# Keep the FastAPI service out of the Vercel build entirely.
#
# Vercel's import screen detects a Python app in backend/ and offers to deploy
# it as a second "service" at /api/backend. That must not happen here: the API
# runs on Render, and a Vercel-side /api/backend route would shadow part of the
# /api/* rewrite in next.config.ts that proxies to it.
#
# vercel.json declaring no `services` key is what actually opts out of that
# behaviour — per Vercel's docs, a project without `services` is evaluated as a
# single ordinary app. This file is the belt to that pair of braces, and it also
# trims the upload: the Next build reads nothing below.
backend/

# Fixtures for scripts/seed.py, which runs from a laptop, never from the build.
sample-docs/

# CI and agent-context files; not build inputs.
.github/
AI_NOTES.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
